window.docContents[28].resolve({"/part-4-frameworks/ch15-permanence-saturation/#ch15-permanence-saturation":{"contents":"While Enlargement simultaneously solves families of constraints over standard entities, many advanced constructions—especially Peter Loeb's measure theory (Ch. 16) and Banach nonstandard hulls (Ch. 18)—require solving families of constraints over already-constructed internal entities.\n\nA framework is \\kappa-saturated if every family \\mathcal{A} of internal sets with the Finite Intersection Property and cardinality |\\mathcal{A}| < \\kappa has nonempty intersection \\bigcap \\mathcal{A} \\neq \\emptyset. In Ch15_PermanenceSaturation.lean (3,156 lines), we prove:\n\n* Permanence Principles (overflow and underflow across \\mathbb{N}, \\mathbb{I}_+, and \\mathbb{L}) and Robinson's Sequential Lemma: if an internal hypersequence (x_N) satisfies x_n \\approx_h 0 for every finite n \\in \\mathbb{N}, then there exists an unlimited \\nu \\in \\mathbb{N}^*_\\infty such that x_N \\approx_h 0 for all N \\le \\nu!* Saturation \\iff Comprehensiveness: Countable (\\aleph_1-) saturation is equivalent to countable comprehensiveness—every sequence f : \\mathbb{N} \\to B into an internal set B extends to an internal function F : {}^*\\mathbb{N} \\to B satisfying F(n) = f(n) for all n \\in \\mathbb{N}.* Exact Cardinalities: Every infinite internal subset of \\mathbb{R}^* has cardinality at least \\aleph_1 (in fact 2^{\\aleph_0}), |\\mathbb{R}^*| = 2^{\\aleph_0} equals the continuum, and therefore \\mathbb{R}^* is \\aleph_1-saturated while not (2^{\\aleph_0})^+-saturated!\n\nsection\nopen Goldblatt.Ch15\n\n#check @permanence_posInfinitesimal_underflow\n#check @countable_saturation_hyperreal_iff_concurrent_internalRel₂\n#check @card_infinite_internal_hyperreal_ge_aleph_one\n#check @card_hyperreal_eq_continuum\n#check @not_succ_continuum_saturated_hyperreal\nend\n\n\n","context":"Lectures on the Hyperreals — Interactive Lean 4 & Spatial Edition\u0009Part IV — Nonstandard Frameworks, Enlargements & Saturation","header":"4.3. Chapter 15: Permanence, Robinson's Lemma &  <missing> -Saturation","id":"/part-4-frameworks/ch15-permanence-saturation/#ch15-permanence-saturation"}});